tSaturday, September 24, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tSince their debut, Whitehorse has traveled from magnetic folk duo to full-blown rock band and beyond. In truth Whitehorse is never fully either one or the other, but an ever-evolving creative partnership that challenges both artists.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWed\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t28\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Paper Kites – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tWednesday, September 28, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tGive them your tired, your lonely, your lovesick, your unsure, The Paper Kites have a song for each of them. “I created a world based on the idea of watching other people, but a lot of the songs are extensions of myself or people I know,” he says.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOctober 2022\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMon\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t3\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Rural Alberta Advantage\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tMonday, October 3, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tThe Rise, the new EP from The Rural Alberta Advantage, is the first word in a conversation, the first step on a new, unkept trail.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$27.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t6\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBasia Bulat\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 6, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tIntroducing The Garden: a STRINGS ALBUM and a RETROSPECTIVE from a room in Montreal with the windows open, and the wind moving, and the leaves changing, and a spring-coloured secret on the tip of Basia Bulat’s tongue.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$27.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t14\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMoontricks – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, October 14, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tCombining their love of folk, blues, and electronic music, Nathan Gurley and Sean Rodman are blazing their own trail, merging musical worlds previously unacquainted and capturing audiences along the way.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$25.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t15\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMoontricks – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, October 15, 2022 at 7:00 pm - 10:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Good Will\t\n\t\n\t\t625 Portage Avenue, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tNestled deep in the beautiful Kootenay mountains of Western Canada lies the home of Moontricks, a duo whose timeless sound captures the essence of their rugged roots.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$25.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t27\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Milk Carton Kids + Katie Pruitt\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 27, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tListening to The Milk Carton Kids — Joey Ryan and Kenneth Pattengale — talk about their creative process, it’s easy to imagine them running in opposite directions even while yoked together. “Joey and I famously have an adversarial relationship,” Pattengale says.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00 – $45.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tNovember 2022\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWed\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLeif Vollebekk\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tWednesday, November 2, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tLeif Vollebekk is a Montreal-adopted singer-songwriter. He will release his highly anticipated fourth full-length album New Ways on November 1st, the follow-up to his breakthrough Polaris Music Prize finalist, Juno-nominated record Twin Solitude. \n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t3\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tFive Alarm Funk\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, November 3, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHot, sweaty dance floors with feet stomping and everybody moving. Grooves for days. Monster horns, crushing percussion and shredding psych-rock guitars.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t4\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tFive Alarm Funk – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, November 4, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHot, sweaty dance floors with feet stomping and everybody moving. Grooves for days. Monster horns, crushing percussion and shredding psych-rock guitars.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t24\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tTim Baker\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, November 24, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tTim Baker is a prolific wild-eyed dreamer. In 2022, Baker has returned with The Festival, a sonic embrace, a call-in for love, and a cry-out for connection.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$33.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t26\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tWilliam Prince\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, November 26, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tWilliam Prince approaches the big questions with humility and curiosity, and his songwriting is a masterclass in skillful simplicity.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$36.00 – $53.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDecember 2022\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t6\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tRuby Waters – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tTuesday, December 6, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHer sound is similar to her journey – eclectic, always evolving, and unfeigned. Hailing from the small town of Shelburne, Ontario and born to two artists, Ruby was immersed in a musician’s world at a young age.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$20.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t10\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tJP Hoe Hoe Hoe – POSTPONED TO DEC. 16\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, December 10, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tThe JP Hoe Hoe Hoe Holiday Show has become a tried and true tradition for so many of us and never fails to sell out quickly! We’re excited to bring this beloved show back for the 17th time to the Burton Cummings Theatre on December 10, 2022. Join us for an unforgettable evening of music and holiday magic!\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$25.50 – $49.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFebruary 2023\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t7\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tHayden\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tTuesday, February 7, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tFor over 25 years Hayden has been making music on his own terms and on his own schedule. The Polaris Prize and Juno nominee has produced, engineered and mixed most of his records at home, creating a world of his own.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$40.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t10\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBruce Cockburn\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, February 10, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tOne of Canada’s finest artists, Bruce Cockburn has enjoyed an illustrious career shaped by politics, spirituality, and musical diversity. His remarkable journey has seen him embrace folk, jazz, rock, and worldbeat styles while travelling to such far-flung places as Guatemala, Mali, Mozambique, and Nepal, and writing memorable songs about his ever-expanding world of wonders.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$39.50 – $69.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t21\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tVance Joy\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tTuesday, February 21, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tCentennial Concert Hall\t\n\t\n\t\t555 Main Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tAustralian indie folk singer/songwriter Vance Joy began his career playing the Melbourne open-mike scene at the end of the 2000s while completing his law degree. Finding success with his intimate Bon Iver-influenced songs, Joy decided to put law on hold and pursue a music career instead.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$54.00 – $89.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMon\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t27\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tOcie Elliott – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tMonday, February 27, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tOcie Elliott pen tunes that feel lived-in. You can hear their memories, experiences, and emotions in the dusty acoustic guitars, the sparse production, and the graceful harmonies between Jon Middleton and Sierra Lundy. Their life together plays out in the music as if projected on the big screen of an old small-town theater.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t28\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tOcie Elliott – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tTuesday, February 28, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tOcie Elliott pen tunes that feel lived-in. You can hear their memories, experiences, and emotions in the dusty acoustic guitars, the sparse production, and the graceful harmonies between Jon Middleton and Sierra Lundy. Their life together plays out in the music as if projected on the big screen of an old small-town theater.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMarch 2023\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t17\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tAndy Shauf\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, March 17, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHailed as “a gifted storyteller” (NPR Music) for 2016’s The Party and 2020’s The Neon Skyline, Shauf writes albums that unfold like short fiction, full of colorful characters, fine details and a rich emotional depth.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$27.50 – $37.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t30\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMatt Andersen and The Big Bottle of Joy\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, March 30, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tClub Regent Event Centre\t\n\t\n\t\t1425 Regent Avenue West, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tWhen Matt Andersen steps on stage, he brings a lifetime of music to every note he plays. His latest album, The Big Bottle of Joy, is all about hard-won celebration; a dozen songs infused with raw blues-rock, rollicking Americana, thoughtful folk, and ecstatic gospel.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.00 – $39.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t30\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tReuben and the Dark\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, March 30, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tReuben and the Dark is the spirited folk-rock outfit led by Reuben Bullock, whose music blends introspective lyrics with the irrepressible pulse and complicit harmonies of his band.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50 – $34.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tApril 2023\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t20\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tDel Barber\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, April 20, 2023 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tWith nominations for JUNO Awards, Western Canadian Music Awards, and Canadian Folk Music Awards - Del Barber has shaped the folk music canon in Canada with five critically acclaimed studio albums under his belt, as well as a myriad of fans.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t