\t\n\tToday\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tUpcoming\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\tUpcoming\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\tSelect date.\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSeptember 2026\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t25\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBahamas\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, September 25 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tJUNO Award-winning Afie Jurvanen, who performs as Bahamas, returns to Winnipeg this September. Bahamas is praised for his exceptional guitar skills, minimalist soulful sound, and clever, honest songwriting. He blends breezy indie pop, folk, country, and soft-soul funk into laid-back, intimate performance.  Full Bio: Afie Jurvanen does not spend too much time in cities these…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$54.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTue\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t29\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tVieux Farka Touré\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tTuesday, September 29 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tCentre Culturel Franco-Manitobain\t\n\t\n\t\t340 Provencher Blvd, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tCo-Presented with Festival du Voyageur Co-presented by the Winnipeg Folk Festival and Festival du Voyageur, this show features one of the world’s most celebrated guitarists. Often called “The Hendrix of the Sahara,” Vieux Farka Touré blends traditional Malian music with blues, rock, and contemporary influences to create a powerful live performance that has earned him…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$37.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOctober 2026\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t9\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tSYML: Solo in North America\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, October 9 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tSYML is the solo venture of Seattle artist Brian Fennell. Welsh for “simple,” SYML makes music that taps into the instincts that drive us toward places of sanctuary, whether that sanctuary is a place or a person. With more than four billion streams, the multi-platinum artist explores grief, loss, mortality, and the passing of time with…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$49.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t15\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMoontricks\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 15 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tBased in the rustic Kootenay Mountains of Western Canada, Nathan Gurley and Sean Rodman of the nationally renowned electro-folk duo Moontricks draw inspiration from the ongoing cycles of the natural world. Blending organic folk, roots rock, and old-time blues with modern electronic production, Moontricks creates a sound that is both timeless and fresh. Throughout the…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$37.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t22\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe East Pointers – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 22 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tJUNO Award-winning band, The East Pointers, are innovators within the ever-evolving world of modern folk. They craft a joy-conjuring, dancefloor-shaking, roof-rattling fusion of folk, pop, and dance music. In the studio, their four records have captured the furious energy of their live shows, adding to the legacy of East Coast folk while lighting a path for…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$44.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t24\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tHawksley Workman Duo\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, October 24 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHawksley Workman is a JUNO Award-winning, Gold Record-certified singer-songwriter and multi-instrumentalist. From his groundbreaking, self-produced indie debut For Him and the Girls (1999) to his chart-topping singles of the 2020s, Workman’s genre-defying style weaves together folk, chart pop, and irrepressible cabaret. His show-stopping vocals and songs about weather, love, heartbreak, and tales of the end…\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPrevious Events\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\tToday\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tNext Events\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\tSubscribe to calendar\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tGoogle Calendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tiCalendar\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook 365\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tOutlook Live\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tExport .ics file\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\tExport Outlook .ics file\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\n\t( function () {\n\t\tvar completed = false;\n\n\t\tfunction initBreakpoints(