:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tPlaskett’s songs are a perennial part of the national playlist, a fixture on “best of” lists, and the soundtrack to the lives of faithful fans across the country and around the world.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t24\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tWhitehorse\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, September 24, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tSince their debut, Whitehorse has traveled from magnetic folk duo to full-blown rock band and beyond. In truth Whitehorse is never fully either one or the other, but an ever-evolving creative partnership that challenges both artists.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWed\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t28\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Paper Kites – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tWednesday, September 28, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tGive them your tired, your lonely, your lovesick, your unsure, The Paper Kites have a song for each of them. “I created a world based on the idea of watching other people, but a lot of the songs are extensions of myself or people I know,” he says.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tOctober 2022\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMon\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t3\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Rural Alberta Advantage\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tMonday, October 3, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tThe Rise, the new EP from The Rural Alberta Advantage, is the first word in a conversation, the first step on a new, unkept trail.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$27.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t6\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBasia Bulat\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 6, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tIntroducing The Garden: a STRINGS ALBUM and a RETROSPECTIVE from a room in Montreal with the windows open, and the wind moving, and the leaves changing, and a spring-coloured secret on the tip of Basia Bulat’s tongue.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$27.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t14\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMoontricks – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, October 14, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tCombining their love of folk, blues, and electronic music, Nathan Gurley and Sean Rodman are blazing their own trail, merging musical worlds previously unacquainted and capturing audiences along the way.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$25.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t15\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tMoontricks – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, October 15, 2022 at 7:00 pm - 10:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Good Will\t\n\t\n\t\t625 Portage Avenue, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tNestled deep in the beautiful Kootenay mountains of Western Canada lies the home of Moontricks, a duo whose timeless sound captures the essence of their rugged roots.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$25.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t27\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Milk Carton Kids + Katie Pruitt\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, October 27, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton Cummings Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t364 Smith Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tListening to The Milk Carton Kids — Joey Ryan and Kenneth Pattengale — talk about their creative process, it’s easy to imagine them running in opposite directions even while yoked together. “Joey and I famously have an adversarial relationship,” Pattengale says.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00 – $45.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tNovember 2022\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tWed\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tLeif Vollebekk\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tWednesday, November 2, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tLeif Vollebekk is a Montreal-adopted singer-songwriter. He will release his highly anticipated fourth full-length album New Ways on November 1st, the follow-up to his breakthrough Polaris Music Prize finalist, Juno-nominated record Twin Solitude. \n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$35.00\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t3\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tFive Alarm Funk\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, November 3, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHot, sweaty dance floors with feet stomping and everybody moving. Grooves for days. Monster horns, crushing percussion and shredding psych-rock guitars.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tFri\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t4\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tFive Alarm Funk – SOLD OUT\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tFriday, November 4, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tHot, sweaty dance floors with feet stomping and everybody moving. Grooves for days. Monster horns, crushing percussion and shredding psych-rock guitars.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$29.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThu\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t24\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tTim Baker\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tThursday, November 24, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tThe Park Theatre\t\n\t\n\t\t698 Osborne Street, Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\tTim Baker is a prolific wild-eyed dreamer. In 2022, Baker has returned with The Festival, a sonic embrace, a call-in for love, and a cry-out for connection.\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\t$33.50\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tSat\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t26\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tWilliam Prince\t\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\tSaturday, November 26, 2022 at 8:00 pm - 11:00 pm\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\n\t\tBurton